  {
    "id": "ffmpeg-iamf-demuxer-uncontrolled-resource-consumption",
    "title": "FFmpeg",
    "subtitle": "Uncontrolled resource consumption in the IAMF demuxer",
    "icon": "other/ffmpeg.png",
    "summary": "FFmpeg through 8.1.2 trusted an attacker-controlled count_label value before checking the available IAMF OBU data. A 17-byte input could consequently trigger a multi-gigabyte allocation during format probing, exhausting process memory or causing an OOM kill.",
